1	line	Player	Can we start observing the penguins?
1	line	Larry	Yes. Let's get in and start observing. You should note down anything interesting the penguins do. I'll include it in my, uh, research.
1	line	Larry	Look, here come two penguins now.
1	line	Player	Aww, they're cute.
1	line	Larry	EVIL. I mean, how fascinating.
0	section	Interacting with the hideout again
1	line	Player	Can we start observing the penguins?
1	line	Larry	Yes. Let's get in and start observing. You should note down anything interesting the penguins do. I'll include it in my, uh, research.
1	line	Larry	Looks like the penguins are on patrol again.
1	line	Player	They're just walking around, Larry.
1	line	Larry	They are organised! ORGANISED I tell you!
0	section	After observing the penguins
1	line	Larry	I knew it. I knew they were up to something! Did you see that? They were patrolling!
1	option	That's crazy!
2	line	Larry	It isn't! They saluted and recognised each other. They're organised!
2	line	Player	It looked like one of them shivered and the other one just walked past. Nothing suspicious there, it is really cold here!
2	line	Larry	I don't care what you think. I know they are doing something. No one ever believes me. But I'll prove them wrong. ALL OF THEM.
2	line	Player	Okay, calm down. What do you think we should do now?
1	option	It did seem rather suspicious.
2	line	Player	It did seem rather suspicious.
2	line	Larry	You believe me?
2	line	Player	Of course! I mean, those penguins were acting quite strangely.
2	line	Larry	No one ever believes me. Can I...hug you?
2	line	Player	Whoa there, I don't think this calls for hugging. What do we do next about the penguins?
2	line	Larry	We need to get closer to the penguins. Infiltrate them. Learn what they are doing.
2	line	Player	How do you plan to do that?
2	line	Larry	We can't discuss it here; there are too many spies. Let's leave the iceberg and then I'll tell you my plans.
2	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Larry again without leaving
1	line	Larry	We must get away from here before we discuss our plans. We don't want to be overheard.
1	action	end
0	section	Planning the infiltration
0	section	Speaking to Larry at the Zoo or Relekka
1	line	Player	How do you plan to infiltrate the penguins?
1	line	Larry	I have altered some designs of clockwork toys to make a clockwork penguin suit. We will use this to infiltrate their ranks.
1	line	Player	What? We'll just set it off walking? What good will that do?
1	line	Larry	No! I'm going to use a spell to shrink you down so you can control it from the inside.
1	line	Player	Wait a minute, why am I being shrunk? Why can't you get in the suit and annoy the penguins?
1	line	Larry	The penguins know my scent. They'd find me out and capture me and...torture me. No, it has to be you.
1	line	Larry	Don't worry. The spell only works if I'm nearby since I have to be constantly casting it. If trouble starts I'll be close by to help.
1	line	Player	Gee, that's comforting.
1	line	Larry	Here's the book. It has my designs and a list of things you need to get. Use your Crafting table at your house to build it, just like regular clockwork toys.
1	action	
1	line	Player	Why do I have to make the suit? I'm tired of doing all the legwork.
1	line	Larry	You have to make it, because since I got fired from the Zoo I've been homeless. Thanks for caring.
1	line	Player	Oh, sorry... Hey, you told me you were on leave to do research!
1	line	Larry	Well...it's permanent leave, and I am doing research! When I used to work at the Zoo, I noticed the penguins doing odd things, like taking notes or timing things. I asked to have my work detail transferred to their cage and I was fired!
1	line	Larry	I'm sure the penguins are behind it. So I kept spying on them and I'll prove everyone wrong!
1	line	Player	So that's why you can't wear the suit? Because you used to work near them?
1	line	Larry	Err, no. I've had a few run-ins since then. But I don't have time for war stories, we need to concentrate on our mission!
1	line	Larry	When you're done making the suit, we'll head back to the iceberg and try it out.
1	action	end
