0	section	Second iceberg visit
1	line	Larry	Look what they did to the bird hide! It's completely destroyed! The savages. The penguins are on to us.
1	option	I don't think it was the penguins.
2	line	Player	I don't think it was the penguins. You can't even make out the prints clearly, it could have been anything.
2	line	Larry	Well of course you can't make out tracks. Penguins walk single file to hide their numbers! They're clever...so very clever.
1	option	It looks like a warning message to keep us away.
2	line	Player	It looks like a warning message to keep us away. I didn't think penguins were violent by nature.
2	line	Larry	Oh, they act like they aren't, but it's all a guise. They wanted to scare us off. We must be on to something.
1	line	Player	Well, there aren't any penguins around now, so we can't try out the suit.
1	line	Larry	But, we were so close to finding out what exactly is going on. It's all ruined now. How will we ever infiltrate them if there are none around to infiltrate?
1	line	Player	There are other penguins. What about the ones at the Zoo? At least we can test the suit on them.
1	line	Larry	OF COURSE! You are brilliant. I should have thought of that. It's where all of this started. Let's return to the Zoo.
1	line	Larry	I can teleport us back to the Zoo. It'll be faster.
1	line	Player	Then why the whole malarkey with the boat?
1	line	Larry	Boat rides lower my stress level.
1	select	Are you ready to go to the Zoo?
1	option	Yes.
2	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Larry	I'm too tired to teleport again. You'll have to get back to the Zoo on your own.
2	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Larry again without leaving
1	line	Larry	I can teleport us back to the Zoo, but you'll have to make your own way back, teleports tire me out.
1	action	end
0	section	Testing the suit at the zoo
0	section	Speaking to Larry at Ardougne Zoo
1	line	Larry	After I put you in the suit, use the little gate in the enclosure to get inside. The zoo keepers won't notice.
1	line	Player	Guess we should try this out. How do you know a shrinking spell, anyway?
1	line	Larry	Well, a while back I was out in the field observing penguins. I worked for the Ardougne Zoo then. I was just quietly observing them when suddenly there was an avalanche.
1	line	Player	Larry, you are one unlucky dude.
1	line	Larry	I'm not done! I was trapped, but a passing old man stopped to help. He said he would shrink me so I could crawl out from under the weight of the snow.
1	line	Larry	Then he taught me the spell in case I would have need of it again.
1	line	Player	Seems like a pretty wise old man.
1	line	Larry	You see, that incident made me start suspecting the penguins, and my further work with them at the Zoo just confirmed it. I'm sure they got me fired. I know too much.
1	line	Player	Right, well we don't have all day. Time to be a penguin!
1	line	Larry	Okay, but remember, if you move too far away from me the spell will break and you'll be normal sized again. Also, if you need to switch back, just ask me and I'll unshrink you.
1	line	Player	Right, right. Let's just get this over with.
1	line	Player	Penguin time!
1	cond	If the player's hands aren't free:
2	line	Larry	You will need your hands free to operate the suit.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player is wearing a cape:
2	line	Larry	You can't wear a cape inside the suit, it might get caught.
2	action	end
1	action	end
0	section	Speaking to Larry while in the suit
1	line	Larry	Don't talk to me while you're in the suit! It'll give away your cover. Here, I'll get you out of it.
1	action	end
0	section	Using Larry's Tuxedo-time while in the suit
1	line	Player	Okay, I'm ready to be big again! Please get me out of this.
1	line	Larry	All right, keep calm. One growth spurt coming up.
1	action	end
0	section	Entering the cage as a "penguin"
1	line	Player	Squack! Quack, quackity squack, squee.
1	line	Penguin	...
1	line	Penguin	What do you think you are doing?
1	line	Player	I'm, uh, speaking penguin, I think.
1	line	Player	WAIT. How come you can speak in the common tongue? You're a penguin!
1	line	Penguin	...So are you.
1	line	Penguin	And you are speaking in the common tongue. So, what is your point?
1	line	Player	Oh, right. Yes, of course! Uh, I was just, uh, testing you. Making sure you're on your toes, claws, whatever.
1	line	Penguin	Operatives must not speak without giving the proper greeting. You have not given the proper greeting and until you do I have nothing more to say.
1	line	Player	I better try and get this greeting right.
1	action	
1	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
2	line	Penguin	I am sorry comrade, but you still have not shown me the proper greeting.
2	action	end
1	cond	After one out of three correct moves:
2	line	Player	*Whew, that was right. Two more moves to do. If I get those right, he should speak to me.*
2	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
3	action	above
2	cond	After two out of three correct moves:
3	line	Player	*I just need to do one more move and I'll have gotten the greeting right.*
3	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
4	action	above
3	cond	After a full proper greeting:
4	line	Penguin	Welcome comrade. Now we may speak properly.
4	line	Penguin	What news do you bring? Have you made progress with the main directive?
4	line	Player	Uh, the main directive? Yeah...sure, I made progress with it. It was...easy?
4	line	Penguin	It was easy!? It was easy to learn how to FLY?
4	line	Player	Uh, yeah. I just kind of jumped off a hill and flapped a lot.
4	line	Penguin	You flapped a lot? I didn't think we could fly like other birds.
4	cond	If the player has completed Between a Rock...:
5	line	Player	I also launched myself out of a cannon!
5	line	Penguin	This caused you to fly... ingenious.
4	cond	If the player has completed Enlightened Journey:
5	line	Player	Then I flew in a hot air balloon.
5	line	Penguin	A hot air balloon? This contraption made you fly?
5	line	Penguin	This is very amazing. I will make note of it in my mission report.
4	line	Player	Why is this so important? I mean, we're good swimmers, who cares if we can't fly?
4	line	Penguin	Who cares? It's the entire reason we are in this wretched cage! We need to learn the secrets of flight, and the best way is to get these gullible humans to reveal it to us unwittingly. Blast them and their thumbs.
4	line	Player	You sound kind of bitter.
4	line	Penguin	Yes, I am. I'm tired of observing these humans and being gawked at by nasty little children. I miss the fresh codfish of our motherland.
4	line	Player	Anything I can do?
4	line	Penguin	You could take my mission report back to the outpost for me. I don't want to risk breaking out and blowing our cover.
4	line	Penguin	You should check in with the operatives in Lumbridge before you head to the outpost. They might have some news for you to take as well.
4	action	
4	action	end
0	section	After speaking with Ardougne Zoo's penguins
1	line	Player	The penguin gave me his mission report and told me to go to Lumbridge to speak to the penguins there and then go to 'the outpost'.
1	line	Larry	Lumbridge? There aren't any penguins in Lumbridge. Not that I've seen. Where is this 'outpost'?
1	line	Player	Maybe the penguins in Lumbridge are undercover?
1	line	Player	I didn't find out where their outpost is. I'm hoping the ones in Lumbridge will tell me.
1	line	Player	Seems kind of crazy that these penguins have mission reports and operatives.
1	line	Larry	They're organised little devils. Don't underestimate them.
1	line	Larry	You go on ahead to Lumbridge. I'll meet you there and put you in the suit.
1	line	Player	They don't even have thumbs. How organised can they be?
1	action	end
