0	section	Returning to Larry about a secret phrase
1	line	Player	The penguins won't talk to me without some stupid secret phrase. These penguins are crazy!
1	line	Larry	No, I keep trying to tell you, they aren't crazy, they are dangerous and organised.
1	line	Larry	Well, since the penguin at the Zoo is the only one talking to you, maybe you should ask him.
1	line	Larry	I can teleport us back to the Zoo, but you'll have to make your own way back. Teleports tire me out.
1	action	end
0	section	Asking the Zoo penguin the phrase
1	option	The penguins in Lumbridge refuse to talk to me.
2	line	Player	The penguins in Lumbridge refuse to talk to me. They keep demanding a secret phrase.
2	line	Penguin	So, tell them the phrase. It's not exactly hard to remember. Pescaling Pax has a strange sense of humour.
2	line	Player	Pesca-what?
2	line	Penguin	Pescaling Pax. The Pescallion's son. Well, one of them. He's in charge of research and development at our headquarters.
2	line	Player	Oh, where all of the penguins...I mean us...live?
2	line	Penguin	Comrade! You really do have a funny sense of humour. No, our people live in the great city of Palingrad, of course. Ah, home, I miss it.
2	line	Player	You sound pretty homesick. Can't you go and visit Palingrad?
2	line	Penguin	If only. The Pescallion has declared that until we have finished our research of the southern species and have developed our great plan, we may not return. So I am stuck here observing humans.
2	line	Player	Gee, I sure would like to get back, too. If only you'd tell me the phrase, so I could get the other mission report and move on.
2	line	Penguin	How do you not know the phrase, comrade?
2	option	Uh, I forgot what the phrase was.
3	line	Player	Uh, I forgot what the phrase was.
3	line	Player	That was very careless of you, comrade. But it is your problem, not mine.
2	option	I must have left the outpost before they gave out the phrase.
3	line	Player	I must have left the outpost before they gave out the phrase.
3	line	Penguin	No one left before it was given out. I was one of the first operatives to leave, and I know it.
2	option	Is it Rumpelstiltskin?
3	line	Penguin	What? Comrade, I think you need your head examined when you get back.
2	line	Player	I need that phrase! Isn't there anything you can do?
2	cond	If player is wearing a Ring of Charos:
3	line	Penguin	As you are a comrade, I suppose it is my duty to help you.
3	line	Penguin	The phrase is 'Do not trust the walrus'.
2	cond	With a raw cod in inventory:
3	line	Penguin	I see you have some raw cod with you comrade. I might be willing to exchange information for it, if you are willing.
3	option	Sure!
4	line	Player	Sure!
4	action	
4	line	Penguin	Thank you comrade. This is like a taste of the motherland. The phrase is 'Do not trust the walrus.'
4	action	end
3	option	Hmm, no I'll hang on to it.
4	line	Player	Hmm, no I'll hang on to it.
4	action	end
2	line	Penguin	I am sorry comrade, but I cannot break protocol without good reason.
2	action	end
1	option	Where is the outpost?
2	line	Penguin	Haa haa haa, that is a funny joke. I like your sense of humour comrade. It would be like asking 'Where is the motherland'.
2	line	Player	You mean they aren't the same?
2	line	Penguin	Haa haa haa... oh you have me in stitches.
2	action	end
