0	section	Returning to the "sheep" with the phrase
1	line	Player	Do not trust the walrus.
1	line	Sheep	Fine. What do you want?
1	line	Player	The penguin at the Zoo told me to see if you had any news.
1	line	Sheep	We can't get any news in this field! All these humans keep trying to shear us!
1	line	Sheep	We think the Farmer may be an agent for the other side, trying to have us assassinated by all these foolish humans. If you investigate him for us, we can finish our mission report and you can go on your way.
1	line	Player	You want me to disguise myself as a human and talk to the Farmer? Seems like a tough request. I'll only do it if you tell me how to get to the outpost.
1	line	Sheep	What do you mean 'How to get to the outpost'? Any intelligent penguin knows that.
1	line	Player	Are you calling me dumb? Fine. You can talk to the Farmer yourself, and compromise your mission.
1	line	Sheep	No, no, we'll tell you. You just deal with the Farmer.
1	action	end
0	section	Speaking with Fred
1	line	Fred the Farmer	What are you doing on my land?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I'm looking for something to kill.
1	option	I'm lost.
1	option	I need to talk to you about penguins.
2	line	Player	I need to talk to you about penguins.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	About what now? What do penguins have to do with anything?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Bully Fred
3	line	Player	Hey Fred! You've been messing with the wrong people. You better leave the penguins alone... OR ELSE!
3	line	Fred the Farmer	What are you shouting about? Don't you come into my house shouting at me.
3	line	Player	I mean it Fred, I don't know whose side you're working for, but assassinating the penguin operatives is going to get you in trouble. To think you'd even stoop to sending others to try and 'shear' them. Be careful, or you might find you've been shorn.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Is this some kind of joke? I'm a SHEEP farmer. That means I need to shear sheep. What are these penguins you keep talking about?
3	line	Player	Don't play neutral with me, Fred. I see right through you. You're probably working for the squirrels, aren't you? I'll be watching Fred. I'm always watching.
2	option	Warn Fred
3	line	Player	You know that 'Thing' out in your field? It's two penguins in disguise.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Like I haven't heard that before.
3	line	Player	No really, it is! They're trying to observe humans to learn our weaknesses.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Then why are they disguised as sheep?
3	line	Player	They probably thought they'd blend in better. Anyway, I came to warn you to not annoy them too much. They're funny little guys but they seem to have a grudge against you.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	You talk to these penguins?
3	line	Player	Yes, I have a penguin suit and I know the secret greeting. I'm infiltrating them because this crazy guy Larry is convinced they are trying to take over the world or something.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Look, when these voices in your head start talking to you again, you might want to ignore them.
3	line	Player	HEY! I'm not crazy! Larry's a little left of centre, but I'm just helping him out. The penguins really can talk.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Right, right. I believe you, sure. Maybe on your way out you could ask the sheep to herd themselves for me.
3	line	Player	Fine. Don't believe me. Larry and I will prove you wrong. Just don't go near the penguins, Fred, not if you value your life.
3	action	end
0	section	Reporting back to the "sheep"
1	line	Sheep	Is the Farmer an agent for the other side?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	The farmer is definitely an enemy.
2	line	Player	The Farmer is definitely an enemy. High ranking too, I think. He might even be the King of Lumbridge in disguise!
2	line	Sheep	King? I thought there was a duke, not a king.
2	line	Player	Well, that's why he's in disguise. Duh.
2	line	Sheep	This is an amazing revelation. We must include it in our report. Thank you, we'll mention your bravery.
1	option	The Farmer is harmless.
2	line	Player	The Farmer is harmless. The sheep, however...now they seem pretty crafty.
2	line	Sheep	The sheep? But...They just wander around in this field all day. Trust us, we know.
2	line	Player	Exactly! So you don't suspect them! That's why they are so cunning. Watch your backs.
2	line	Sheep	You have a good point. Yes, we must warn Pescaling Pax of this new threat. We'll put it in the report and you can give it to them.
1	action	
1	line	Sheep	Well, off you go now!
1	line	Player	Hey wait, you said you'd tell me where the outpost is!
1	line	Sheep	You are one clueless penguin. The outpost is the iceberg to the North. The entrance is concealed by what looks like an avalanche.
1	line	Sheep	When you try and go through a guard will stop you and ask for the password.
1	line	Sheep	The password is cabbage. Don't forget it.
1	action	end
0	section	After finding the outpost's location
1	line	Player	Haa haa, this is fun!
1	line	Larry	What? How?
1	cond	If the player told the penguins that Fred is a threat:
2	line	Player	I just convinced them Fred the Farmer was the King of Lumbridge!
2	line	Larry	But there is no King of Lumbridge.
2	line	Player	Exactly! They are so gullible. Even if they are organised.
2	line	Larry	Don't take this so lightly. You might put Fred in danger because you were having a laugh.
2	line	Player	Sorry. It was just a bit of fun.
1	cond	If the player told the penguins that Fred is harmless:
2	line	Player	I just convinced the penguins that the sheep are agents for the other side.
2	line	Larry	They are?
2	line	Player	No! They're just sheep. But I wanted to confuse the penguins. Put them off our scent.
2	line	Larry	What a good plan! I just hope the sheep aren't working for the other side.
2	line	Player	Larry, we need to get you to hang out with people, not animals.
1	line	Player	I know where their outpost is! The entrance is on the iceberg. It's concealed by an avalanche.
1	line	Larry	Great. Let's go back to the iceberg, I'll put you in your suit and we'll really see what these penguins are up to.
1	select	Are you ready to go to the iceberg?
1	option	Yes
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	No.
2	action	end
0	section	Entering the outpost
0	section	Speaking to Larry
1	line	Larry	Now you can try and enter the outpost. This is exciting.
1	line	Player	It's fun for you! You're not risking your neck.
1	line	Larry	But you don't think penguins are dangerous anyway. So there's no danger is there? Or are you coming around to my thinking that they are dangerous?
1	line	Player	No...I mean...yes. Oh never mind. Just do the spell. Wait, won't the spell wear off once I'm inside? You'll be too far away.
1	line	Larry	Oh, no. The ice magnifies this spell, so it will allow you to go greater distances.
1	action	end
0	section	In front of the entrance
1	line	Player	This guy looks official. I'd better do the greeting before I speak to him.
1	action	
1	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
2	line	KGP Agent	Don't stand around, agent. You look absurd.
1	cond	After one out of three correct moves:
2	line	Player	*Whew, that was right. Two more moves to do. If I get those right, he should speak to me.*
2	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
3	action	above
2	cond	After two out of three correct moves:
3	line	Player	*I just need to do one more move and I'll have gotten the greeting right.*
3	cond	If the player fails the greeting:
4	action	above
3	cond	After a full proper greeting:
4	line	KGP Agent	Password?
4	line	Player	Cabbage.
4	line	KGP Agent	Let's see your ID and you can go through.
4	line	Player	ID? No one told me anything about ID.
4	line	KGP Agent	No ID, no entry!
4	action	end
0	section	Asking Larry about an ID
1	line	Player	The penguin at the entrance said I needed to have an ID. Nobody told me about any ID!
1	line	Larry	ID? But...they all look alike. Well, the other penguins probably just assumed you had it, since you said you were an agent.
1	line	Larry	You know, I met a rather shifty looking penguin once, north of Miscellania. He was named after some sort of pasta...
1	line	Larry	Anyway, he worked for a black market. Maybe he has a contact here who could get you an ID?
1	line	Player	Penguins have black markets?
1	line	Larry	Of course. Just look around here for a shifty pasta penguin.
1	action	end
0	section	Obtaining an ID from the black market
1	line	Noodle	Oi, mate, 'u innerested i' sum 'wares?
1	line	Player	Uh...maybe?
1	line	Noodle	I go' me sum hot 'wares, mate. Wotcha need?
1	line	Player	Well, I've misplaced me, I mean my, ID card.
1	line	Noodle	Ah, frisky nigh' on leave, eh? Betcha furgo' yur missin repor' 'oo.
1	line	Player	Yeah, my missin repor'. I think I need one of them too.
1	line	Noodle	Well, mate. 'U scratch me back, I stab urs, right?
1	line	Player	What? No, no stabbing.
1	line	Noodle	I men' in a good way. I wan' sumpin in exy-change. Ima in need of sum swamp tur.
1	line	Player	Tur? Do you mean tar?
1	line	Noodle	Thas wha' I sed, innit? I need sum feathers 'oo. Foive of 'em.
1	line	Player	So you need swamp tar and five feathers. Will chicken feathers do?
1	line	Noodle	Yea, begreat. Then I'll guv yea 'ur stuff.
1	action	end
