0	section	Upon entering
0	section	Inside the outpost
0	section	Debriefing
1	line	KGP Agent	Welcome back agent...
1	cond	If the player character is male:
2	line	KGP Agent	Peach? But, aren't you...male?
2	line	Player	It was either that or Pear.
2	line	KGP Agent	Ah. Of course.
1	cond	If the player character is female:
2	line	KGP Agent	Pablo? But, aren't you...female?
2	line	Player	Hippie parents, sir. They had weird ideas about names.
1	line	KGP Agent	So you have just returned from your mission?
1	line	Player	Yes, and I have my mission report. I also have the mission reports from the operatives in the Ardougne Zoo and the Lumbridge sheep field.
1	line	KGP Agent	How very industrious of you, agent. Please hand them over.
1	action	
1	line	KGP Agent	Hmm, these reports are...intriguing.
1	line	KGP Agent	It says you jumped off a hill and flew? Without assistance?
1	line	Player	Oh yeah. It was amazing. You know, I just...flapped. Really fast.
1	line	KGP Agent	Hmm, we shall have to research this.
1	cond	If the player has completed Between a Rock...:
2	line	KGP Agent	Did you really get launched out of a cannon? It seems quite risky.
2	line	Player	It wasn't too bad. I was wearing a helmet at the time.
2	line	KGP Agent	This could be very useful during battle.
1	cond	If the player has completed Enlightened Journey:
2	line	KGP Agent	You flew in a 'hot air balloon'? What is that exactly?
2	line	Player	Well, it was a sack of cloth with a basket attached to the bottom and when you filled it with hot air it went up.
2	line	KGP Agent	Fascinating. Well done agent.
1	line	KGP Agent	I am satisfied with your reports. You just need to complete a physical and you will be free to roam at your leasure.
1	line	Player	A physical? What, are they going to examine my body?
1	line	KGP Agent	Oh no. It's an agility course to make sure you're still fit and able to serve. Don't worry, I'm sure you won't have any difficulty getting through it. Just go through the door at the end of the room.
1	action	end
0	section	Finishing the agility course
1	line	Agility Instructor	Well done soldier! You've successfully completed the physical. You're free to do as you like.
1	line	Player	What do I do now?
1	line	Agility Instructor	Just go through the gate in the fence and use the same door you came out of. You can come back whenever you like to tone up your body.
1	action	end
0	section	Speaking with the army commander outside the course
1	line	Player	All those penguins, what are they doing?
1	line	Army Commander	Ah, they are doing drills! Getting ready for the invasion. What a glorious day that will be!
1	line	Player	Invasion? Of...
1	line	Army Commander	Yes, yes, I know we all get excited. But, I need you to get out of the way. Move along!
1	action	end
0	section	Reporting to Larry after finding about penguin training
1	line	Player	Larry, you were right! There's an entire army of them, and they're drilling and... Larry, they're ORGANISED!
1	line	Larry	That's what I've been saying from the start! But an entire army? This is just an outpost, so it can't be an entire army.
1	line	Player	I know what I saw! They were doing drills and everything.
1	line	Larry	Still, it must only be an invasion party. The main force is on...well, it doesn't matter right now.
1	line	Larry	I've been doing some research of my own, and I think I know what our next step should be. There's a secret room, deep in the glacier. I think that is where they are making their war plans.
1	line	Player	War plans! Who are they going to war with?
1	line	Larry	With us, you dolt! They are trying to take over the world. Have you not grasped this yet? You need to find that room. Our future depends on it.
1	line	Player	Where could this room be?
1	line	Larry	It's probably the most well guarded room in the place. You'll need to find a way to get into it without arousing suspicion.
1	line	Player	That's a pretty tall order.
1	action	end
0	section	Searching for the secret room
0	section	Speaking to Larry again before looking for the war room
1	line	Larry	What are you doing out here! You need to get in there and find the secret room.
1	line	Player	Keep your shorts on; I'm working on it.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the agent near the large door
1	line	Player	You there, let me through those doors.
1	line	KGP Agent	Let's see your ID, comrade.
1	line	Player	No problem!
1	line	KGP Agent	I'm sorry comrade, you do not have the clearance to go through these doors.
1	action	end
0	section	Asking penguins in a room nearby about the door
1	line	Player	You look like...knowledgeable...penguins. What's through those doors at the end of the hall?
1	line	Pong	Hey man, don't stress. Those doors open new worlds, man. Like, new rooms too.
1	line	Player	Yes, well, I would like to know what rooms.
1	line	Ping	Like, the War Room and stuff like that, dude. Wicked stuff. Too bad only 'the man' gets to go through.
1	line	Player	Humans can go through?
1	line	Pong	No, man. He just means the authority. The MAN, you know?
1	line	Player	Who are you? You don't really look like KGP agents.
1	line	Ping	Dude, we are bards. We sing of the glories of the common penguin. We are also supposed to record history, but man, it is so HIS story. Like, the MAN's story.
1	line	Player	Penguins have bards?
1	line	Ping	Totally, dude. You want to hear one of our songs?
1	line	Player	Sure, I haven't got anything to lose, except my eardrums.
1	line	Pong	Well, like, we can't play it in THIS now. Maybe at a later now. We don't have any instruments to accompany our great song.
1	line	Player	But this room is filled with instruments.
1	line	Pong	Yeah man, but they come from the south, where humans have thumbs to play them with. We don't have thumbs. Also, the Pescaling had our old ones confiscated for being too loud.
1	line	Player	Way harsh, man.
1	line	Ping	But dude, I was reading, and there are instruments we could play. I read about one called bongos. They just need to be hit.
1	line	Pong	But we need two instruments, man. Like, to make it harmonious with the vibes.
1	line	Player	What about a cowbell? You don't need thumbs for that.
1	line	Pong	Righteous man. So you'll get a cowbell and bongos for us and we'll rock out. We'll be so harmonious, no Pescallion could complain.
1	line	Player	Wait, why am I getting these instruments?
1	line	Pong	Because your aura says you should.
1	action	end
0	section	Asking Larry about the cowbell and bongos
1	line	Player	I think I have a lead. These two penguin bards seem to know a lot of the history of the iceberg. I think they might know a way into the War Room.
1	line	Larry	Bards? They have bards?
1	line	Player	Yeah, that's what I said.
1	line	Player	Where would I get a cowbell or a set of bongos?
1	line	Larry	I'm not even going to ask why.
1	line	Larry	I think dairy cows have bells, you could steal one from it. Bongos... I suppose you could make them? Mahogany is good for bending, and then just use soft leather for the drum.
1	line	Player	Good plan, Larry.
1	action	end
0	section	The iceberg's history song
1	line	Pong	Man, did you bring the instruments to us?
1	option	What did I need to get you?
2	line	Player	What did I need to get you?
2	line	Pong	We want a cowbell and a set of bongos.
2	action	end
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Yes.
